    <string name="ripdpi_seqovl_available_title">Sequence overlap available</string>
    <string name="ripdpi_seqovl_available_body">Use seqovl when the device supports the packet-owned backend. Until then, stored seqovl steps stay round-trippable but fall back to split at runtime.</string>
    <string name="ripdpi_seqovl_ready_title">Sequence overlap configured</string>
    <string name="ripdpi_seqovl_ready_body">The saved bypass strategy already contains seqovl and will preserve its marker, overlap size, and fake mode across settings edits.</string>
    <string name="ripdpi_seqovl_restart_title">Restart to reapply seqovl</string>
    <string name="ripdpi_seqovl_restart_body">The running RIPDPI session started before this chain change, so seqovl will not take effect until RIPDPI reconnects or restarts.</string>
    <string name="ripdpi_seqovl_unsupported_title">Sequence overlap unavailable</string>
    <string name="ripdpi_seqovl_unsupported_body">This device does not expose the packet-owned upstream TCP backend that seqovl needs. New seqovl controls stay disabled and stored seqovl steps degrade to split.</string>
